 grid.\n4. Fill the background cells in that expanded area with the marker colour.\n\nEach framed block is one emitted stage.\n\n**Test input:**\n- The top‑left block (one 1) gets a 1‑wide frame of 1.\n- The top‑right block (two 3s) gets a 2‑wide frame of 3.\n- The lower block (five 6s) gets a 5‑wide frame of 6, covering rows 10–25 and columns 1–17.\n\nThe frames around the two upper blocks do not touch each other or the 6 frame. The 6 frame starts at row 10, and the upper blocks plus their frames end by row 8.","code":"import collections\n\ndef transform(grid):\n    import collections\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg, multicolour=True):\n        cols = collections.Counter(int(g[y, x]) for y, x in o[\"cells\"])\n        if len(cols) < 2:\n            continue\n        (main, _), (mk, k) = cols.most_common(2)\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        Y0, X0 = max(0, y0 - k), max(0, x0 - k)\n        Y1, X1 = min(H - 1, y1 + k), min(W - 1, x1 + k)\n        region = out[Y0:Y1 + 1, X0:X1 + 1]\n        region[region == bg] = mk\n        emit(out, f\"Block of colour {main} has {k} marker(s) of colour {mk}: frame it with a {k}-wide border of colour {mk}.\")\n    emit(out, \"All blocks framed.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"For each multicolour object, count the colours of its cells."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"dominant colour as the block colour and the second colour as the marker, with k equal to the marker count."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Expand the bounding box by k on every side, clipped to the grid."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"ca3cc40f6e88b605eec971aef8a7084623f188a6907340b8ffbfcaa7c5145cf9","task_sha256":"7044397df353bca62c1d2ee375d6910cd75007c518fcccf25d05bb3088ea7f2a","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded 